UID:d99f3bb9c3187444@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 6:00 PM · 7:00 PM–7:45 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 6:00 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 5:45 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT I Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Rats: Rats — Costume (you provide): Male: Black tights\, black fit
 ted t-shirt Female: Black Seamless Tights\, Black or Flesh tone Camisole
  Leotard\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair
 : Male: Hair out of the eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (B
 A provides): Gloves\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Powd
 er matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow applied to the crea
 se with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black
  mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply
  plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• 
  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tight
 s and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle
  costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate f
 abrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume 
 damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Ne
 ver throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by the
 ir elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in co
 stume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any c
 ostume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume 
 and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume du
 ring its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or colog
 ne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast
  member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in cost
 ume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from t
 heir assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bob
 by pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• 
  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with
  any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do
  not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage 
 or stain costumes.
